{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c57b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d1b0-8de1-7d92-b557-e0145e16dab5"},"sequence":280,"recorded_at":1780531400000555,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cf8f870b-7b13-4d13-bdaa-1af4a685e1f8","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"cf8f870b-7b13-4d13-bdaa-1af4a685e1f8","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cf8f870b-7b13-4d13-bdaa-1af4a685e1f8"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0d1b1-3da8-7970-9ce3-e9010e61f8d5"},"task_id":"01a0d1b1-3da8-7970-9ce3-e9010e61f8d5","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0d1b1-3da8-7970-9ce3-e9010e61f8d5","chunk":"Read text file `.temp/TASK-260830-1jmmqn/rev4/results-prev.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1jmmqn results: projection-plan schemas (rework rev2)\n2|\n3|Candidate: UNCOMMITTED tree in the STORY-260830-21bxa3 worktree.\n4|Scope: `internal/cloneplan` (new files only; no landed file edited,\n5|no registry edit). Change Request is `task_delta`. Base trunk\n6|`547ea28` (no refresh needed: checkpoint descends from trunk).\n7|\n8|This revision answers all four rev1 findings\n9|(`member-case-variant-uncounted`, `dag-large-invalid-uncounted`,\n10|`entry-presence-combinations-uncounted`,\n11|`exact-tree-diff-check-missed`) plus the two rev1 notes (1M\n12|mapping entry edge, importer triple key). No production file\n13|changed semantics: every rev1 production line is intact; the diff\n14|is tests + harness + TRACEABILITY.\n15|\n16|## What changed per finding\n17|\n18|1. Census derived from the Go types (`members_test.go`\n19|   rewritten): a reflection walk over both input types (nested\n20|   structs, slices of structs, maps; unhandled kinds fail loudly)\n21|   yields every shape member with its JSON type and nullability via\n22|   a mechanical snake_case rule plus 4 documented irregular names\n23|   (`expected_target_native_session_id`, `target_resource_keys`,\n24|   `expected_disposition`, `insertion_after_event_id`); synthesized\n25|   top-level members derive by sealed set difference; the exact-set\n26|   test cross-checks derived vs sealed in both directions.\n27|   Miscased sweep covers 6 variant classes (upper, lower,\n28|   title-first, title-segments, toggle-first, toggle-last);\n29|   duplication surgery covers EVERY member via a byte-path splicer.\n30|   `TestMemberCensusNoLiteralList` guards the derivation (AST scan\n31|   trips at 10+ member names, 40%+ purity; a planted 12-name list\n32|   reddened it and removal greened it). The reviewer's Titlecase\n33|   plant is killed by `TestMemberCensusMiscased` ALONE (adopted as\n34|   harness row `N-case-title-strategy`, byte-identical edit).\n35|2. DAG whole domain (`dag_test.go` rewritten):\n36|   `TestDAGWholeDomainCensus` classifies EVERY graph through 4\n37|   operations (2+16+512+65536) against the oracle through both\n38|   entries, and at 5 operations drives every edge class\n39|   (self/equal, higher, lower, missing, unsorted, duplicate) at\n40|   every position. `TestDAGValidEnumerationFive` admits all 1024\n41|   valid 5-DAGs; `TestDAGSingleEdgeLocality` (35 toggles) and\n42|   `TestDAGLocalityStructure` (AST pin: 3 range loops, calls subset\n43|   of make/len/invalid, `>=` lower rule, single presence store,\n44|   negated lookup) prove the per-edge-local rule. The reviewer's\n45|   4-op self-edge plant is killed by the census ALONE (adopted as\n46|   `N-dagfour-self`, byte-identical edit).\n47|3. Entry grid (`nullability_test.go` rewritten):\n48|   `TestEntryNullabilityGrid` sweeps kind x all 2^3 presence\n49|   combinations x mode (48 cells) through BOTH manifest entries\n50|   against the oracle; every refuse cell asserts a structural\n51|   literal (branch phrases on build, unknown/missing member codes\n52|   on decode, which fire before the self-digest check).\n53|   `TestEntryGridNeverPanics` sweeps the same grid under per-cell\n54|   recovery. The reviewer's branchcombo plant is killed by the\n55|   grid ALONE via the panic guard (adopted as\n56|   `N-entry-branch-combo`, byte-identical edit). Production keeps\n57|   no redundant nil checks: they would mask the shipped\n58|   single-member branch narrowings.\n59|4. Hygiene: the harness EOF blank line is removed; the scratch-\n60|   index `git diff --cached --check` over the full candidate\n61|   (tracked + untracked, real index untouched) exits 0.\n62|5. Notes closed: `TestMappingCountMillionEntryLevel` seals and\n63|   decodes exactly 1,000,000 mappings and refuses 1,000,001 with\n64|   the count literal on BOTH entries (31s; skips under\n65|   `-short` like the 65536 precedent); `N-count-mapping-max` now\n66|   kills at the entry test. The importer grid is keyed\n67|   (package, entry, input): 22 reused owner entries x input\n68|   classes, base vs candidate, with 171 files hash-compared\n69|   identical and owner suites green on both trees — no moved\n70|   class. The build zero census extends to nested plan members\n71|   with reflection-count guards on every table.\n72|\n73|## AC coverage, measured: 18 of 18 leaf-schema rows driven\n74|\n75|Denominator: the 18 leaf-schema rows (planning semantics excluded\n76|per the orchestrator split). Each row names its production call\n77|site; every refusal below is literal-pinned and every gate carries\n78|a killed narrowing (matrix names them).\n79|\n80|| # | Row | Call site | Test |\n81||---|---|---|---|\n82|| 1 | Plan 36-member set + schema/version literals | D | Derived census + UnknownMissing + Miscased(6 classes) + WrongTypes + Duplicated(every member) + NoLiteralList + SchemaLiterals |\n83|| 2 | `projection_plan_id` omit-self identity | B, D | TestPlanIdentityIndependent |\n84|| 3 | Mapping shape + disposition/reason vocabs | B, D | Census + ExpectedDisposition/MappingReason oracles |\n85|| 4 | Operation shape + sequence order | B, D | Census + DAGRefusalLiterals |\n86|| 5 | Dependency DAG vs oracle | B, D (shared gate) | WholeDomainCensus + ValidFive + Locality + SingleEdge + RefusalLiterals |\n87|| 6 | Resource branch-exact nullability | B, D (shared gate) | ResourceNullabilityGrid (12/12 full) + BranchLiterals |\n88|| 7 | Synth event shape + purposes | B, D | Census + SynthesizedPurposeOracle |\n89|| 8-11 | Transaction/ReadBack/Resume/Rollback constants | B, D | TestPlanConstants + NestedPlans zero cells |\n90|| 12 | ContractRequirement (id, SemVer, no ext) | B, D | TestContractSemver + TestContractNoExtensions |\n91|| 13 | Manifest 10-member set + identity | MB, MD | Derived census + SchemaLiterals + ManifestIdentityIndependent |\n92|| 14 | Entry branch-exact member sets | MB, MD | EntryNullabilityGrid (48/48 full) + GridNeverPanics + EntryBranchLiterals |\n93|| 15 | Sorting/uniqueness on every ordered array | B, D, MB, MD | TestSortedUniqueSweep + TestRowOrderSweep |\n94|| 16 | Every bound at edge and edge+1 | B, D, MB, MD | CountEdges + MillionEntryLevel + FactoredCountGates + String/Number edges |\n95|| 17 | Policy maps | B, D | TestRequiredDispositions + TestSecurityExclusions |\n96|| 18 | Scalar delegation | B, D, MB, MD | TestScalarGates + TestManifestScalarGates + TestNumberModel |\n97|\n98|Stated bounds (not waived): 5-op DAG coverage is structural (33M\n99|graphs infeasible); the literal-list guard trips at census scale\n100|(10+/40%+); JSON-level member probes run at decode entries while\n101|build runs the per-field zero census (Go inputs cannot express\n102|extra/duplicated/wrong-typed members). Cross-artifact couplings,\n103|`total_bytes` derivation, and synthesized order stay bounded as in\n104|rev1 (TRACEABILITY).\n105|\n106|## Out-of-contract rows (declared, not silent)\n107|\n108|- \"Plan pair-neutral target projection, checkpoint message\n109|  authority, inactive tools/instructions, token metadata, and\n110|  vendor importer strategies\" as PLANNING SEMANTICS: sibling leaf\n111|  TASK-260924-3n78rv (orchestrator split); this leaf gates shapes\n112|  only. No planning-semantics code was added.\n113|- Cross-artifact couplings, `total_bytes` derivation, synthesized\n114|  array order, policy key closure: stated bounds in TRACEABILITY.md\n115|  (spec-silent or sibling-input scope), each witnessed by a named\n116|  test.\n117|\n118|## Brief gap (handoff precondition 1)\n119|\n120|The brief carries no surface table, so there is no surface row to\n121|map. Coverage map substitute: the clause map in\n122|`internal/cloneplan/TRACEABILITY.md` maps every pinned clause to\n123|its production entries and named tests, and the conformance matrix\n124|(`TASK-260830-1jmmqn_conformance-matrix.md`) maps every gate to\n125|its entries, killer tests, and killed narrowings (123 narrowings +\n126|1 marked arm-delete + 1 control).\n127|\n128|## Validation (real exit codes)\n129|\n130|| Command | Exit | Evidence |\n131||---|---|---|\n132|| `go test -count=1 ./internal/cloneplan/` | 0 (47s) | `package.log` |\n133|| `go test -count=1 -cover ./internal/cloneplan/` | 0, 96.8% statements | `cover.log` |\n134|| `go test -count=1 ./...` (full configured suite, once) | 0, 46 packages ok | `full.log` |\n135|| `go test -count=3` (new/rewritten tests) | 0 (148s) | `determinism.log` |\n136|| `go vet ./internal/cloneplan/` | 0 | `vet.log` |\n137|| `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...` | 0 | `winvet.log` |\n138|| `gofmt -l internal/cloneplan/` | 0, no files | `gofmt.log` |\n139|| Mutant battery, 125 rows, run 1 | 124 KILLED + control SURVIVED | `mut-run1-verdicts.txt`, `mut-logs-run1/` |\n140|| Mutant battery, 125 rows, run 2 | 124 KILLED + control SURVIVED | `mut-run2-verdicts.txt`, `mut-logs-run2/` |\n141|| Owner suites, candidate (6 pkgs) | 0 | `owners-candidate.log` |\n142|| Owner suites, base archive (6 pkgs) | 0 | `owners-base.log` |\n143|| Owner byte-identity base vs candidate | identical, 171 files | `byte-identity.txt` |\n144|| Scratch-index `git diff --cached --check` (full tree) | 0 | `diff-check.log` |\n145|| `task-board.config.json` vs base | byte-identical | `cmp` in run log |\n146|\n147|## Rework diff bound\n148|\n149|The diff touches only `internal/cloneplan/*` (new package; still\n150|uncommitted; real index untouched). No file outside it is listed:\n151|rev1 production semantics are unchanged, and this revision adds no\n152|planning-semantics code, no registry edit, and no landed-file edit.","final_result":true}}}
