{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c931","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d1b0-8de1-7d92-b557-e0145e16dab5"},"sequence":755,"recorded_at":1780531400001505,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cf8f870b-7b13-4d13-bdaa-1af4a685e1f8","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"cf8f870b-7b13-4d13-bdaa-1af4a685e1f8","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cf8f870b-7b13-4d13-bdaa-1af4a685e1f8"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0d1b4-9346-72d1-9027-015fc2c0f536"},"task_id":"01a0d1b4-9346-72d1-9027-015fc2c0f536","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0d1b4-9346-72d1-9027-015fc2c0f536","chunk":"Read text file `internal/cloneplan/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n(99 line(s) above)\n100|| 13.14.2 cardinality bounds at edge/edge+1 | factored count gates + both entries | `TestCountEdges` (entry reachability + 64/65 + 129 + 65536/65537) + `TestFactoredCountGates` (6 gates x min/max/min-1/max+1) + `TestMappingCountMillionEntryLevel` (1M admit + 1M+1 refuse, both entries) |\n101|| 13.14.2 Transaction/ReadBack/Resume/Rollback constants refused on any other value | build + decode per component | `TestPlanConstants` (every member incl. near-miss X2 values, every modes shape, every flag, bounded both booleans + 5 non-boolean refusals) |\n102|| 13.14.2 ContractRequirement (contract_id, SemVer; no extensions) | build + decode | `TestContractSemver` (5 admit + 7 refusals x 2 entries), `TestContractNoExtensions` |\n103|| 13.14.2 required_dispositions exact policy from request | build + decode policy gates | `TestRequiredDispositions` (empty + 5 bad shapes x 2 entries + full 7-set admission) |\n104|| 13.14.2 security_exclusions sorted unique capture-class[0..9] | build + decode | `TestSecurityExclusions` (9 admit, 10-count, vocab refusal x 2 entries) + `TestSortedUniqueSweep` |\n105|| 13.14.2 scalar gates (digests, UUIDv7, tuples, workspace, limits) | both entries via landed owners | `TestScalarGates` (14 decode + 11 build rows), `TestManifestScalarGates` (3+3 rows) |\n106|| 13.14.2 AX number model (no fractions/exponents/strings/≥2^53) | decode via `environ.CheckUint53Bounds`; build overflow checks | `TestNumberModel` (6 members x 6 bad values + max admit + 6 build overflows) |\n107|| 13.14.2 closed extensions (reverse-DNS keys, AX values, no nested dup) | both entries via `clonebundle` owner | `TestExtensionsClosed` (admission + build/decode rows + nested dup) |\n108|| 13.14.2 strict framing (dup/trailing/non-object/surrogate/UTF-8) | `decodeStrictObject` | `TestFraming` (9 plan + 3 manifest + 1 surrogate rows) |\n109|| 13.14.2 build UTF-8 pre-marshal gate (every string-valued member refuses invalid UTF-8; decode refuses at the delegated strict frame before dispatch) | build string admissions; decode via `decodeStrictObject` | `TestUTF8RefusalReflectionGrid` (72 reflection-derived members x 5 invalid-UTF-8 classes x both entries) + `TestRegistryPredicatesRefuseInvalidUTF8` (5 predicates x 5 classes) |\n110|| 13.14.2 build-side member census (every input member zeroed) | both build entries | `TestBuildZeroValueCensus` (33 plan cells, 6 admit), `TestBuildZeroValueRows` (mapping/operation/resource/event/contract), `TestBuildZeroValueNestedPlans` (transaction/read-back/resume/rollback members), `TestBuildZeroValueManifest` (top/entry); every table asserts its cell count against the reflected field count |\n111|| 13.14.2 determinism (identical inputs, identical bytes) | both build entries | `TestDeterminism` (10 builds byte-identical per entry) |\n112|| 13.14.2 purity (no durable write) | all four entries | `TestEntriesArePure` (decode never mutates input; every build output decodes clean) |\n113|\n114|## Durability\n115|\n116|This package holds no local state and performs no durable write:\n117|sealing is pure bytes (`json.Marshal` + JCS + SHA-256 over memory),\n118|so crash semantics are vacuous. The durability proof is\n119|determinism plus purity: `TestDeterminism` (ten builds\n120|byte-identical per entry) and `TestEntriesArePure` (decode never\n121|mutates its input; every build output decodes clean).\n122|\n123|## Mutants\n124|\n125|`testdata/mutant_harness.py` ships 123 narrowing rows, one\n126|token-preserving arm-delete row (`N-dag-locality-evasion`, marked\n127|NOT a narrowing in its note), and the harmless `C-doc-comment`\n128|SURVIVED control. Every narrowing weakens one gate to admit exactly\n129|one member of the class it must reject, and every killer drives a\n130|production entry alone. Shared gates (one implementation, two call\n131|sites: the vocabulary predicates, the strict frame, the member\n132|census helpers, the order helpers, the DAG gate, the branch gates,\n133|the factored count gates, the modes constant, the build UTF-8\n134|helpers) carry one plant each with a killer that drives the\n135|production entries; rules implemented twice (build + decode) carry\n136|one plant per side. `N-strategy-route` and `N-action-route` are the\n137|token-preserving attacks: the searched-for token still matches\n138|while the decision changes, and the killers execute the behavioral\n139|oracle suites through both entries. Single-member-class rows label\n140|gates whose reject class holds exactly one member. The battery runs\n141|twice with one raw log per plant per run carrying the subprocess\n142|exit.\n143|\n144|## Importer outcome grid\n145|\n146|This leaf adds `internal/cloneplan` (new files only) and edits no\n147|landed file: the six reused owner packages are byte-identical\n148|between base and candidate (171 files, hash-compared), and their\n149|suites are green on both trees, so no input class moved. The grid\n150|below is keyed (package, entry, input): one row per reused owner\n151|entry with the input classes flowing through this leaf's call\n152|sites, plus this leaf's own new entries. Base is trunk HEAD\n153|(`547ea28`); candidate is the uncommitted tree.\n154|\n155|| Package | Entry | Input classes through this leaf | Base | Candidate | Moved |\n156||---|---|---|---|---|---|\n157|| `internal/environ` | `DecodeStrictObject` | valid object docs; dup-member / trailing-data / non-object / surrogate-escape docs | green | green | none |\n158|| `internal/environ` | `StringLength` | ASCII + multibyte strings at every bound | green | green | none |\n159|| `internal/environ` | `CheckStringBounds` | in-bound; over-max / under-min; non-string JSON | green | green | none |\n160|| `internal/environ` | `CheckUint53Bounds` | in-bound uint53; fraction / exponent / string / 2^53 | green | green | none |\n161|| `internal/environ` | `CheckDigest` | valid sha256; malformed digests | green | green | none |\n162|| `internal/environ` | `CheckUUIDv7` | valid v7; v4 / malformed ids | green | green | none |\n163|| `internal/environ` | `CheckSortedUniqueStrings` | sorted-unique; unsorted / duplicated / over-count | green | green | none |\n164|| `internal/environ` | `CheckSortedUniqueDigests` | sorted-unique; unsorted / duplicated | green | green | none |\n165|| `internal/environ` | `CheckSemver` | valid SemVer; non-SemVer versions | green | green | none |\n166|| `internal/scalar` | `ParseDigest` | valid sha256; malformed digests | green | green | none |\n167|| `internal/scalar` | `ParseUUIDv7` | valid v7; malformed ids | green | green | none |\n168|| `internal/scalar` | `SHA256Digest` | canonical omit-self bytes | green | green | none |\n169|| `internal/canonicaljson` | `Canonicalize` | plan / manifest / row objects | green | green | none |\n170|| `internal/clonebundle` | `EncodeExtensions` | closed maps; bad keys / values | green | green | none |\n171|| `internal/clonebundle` | `CheckExtensionsClosed` | closed; open / nested-dup | green | green | none |\n172|| `internal/clonebundle` | `OmitSelfDigest` | member maps + self field; tampered claims | green | green | none |\n173|| `internal/clonebundle` | `DecodeWorkspaceBinding` | valid bindings; broken bindings | green | green | none |\n174|| `internal/clonebundle` | `ValidCaptureClass` | 9 classes; unknown / 10th | green | green | none |\n175|| `internal/sessadapter` | `DecodeTuple` | valid tuples; broken tuples | green | green | none |\n176|| `internal/sessadapter` | `DecodeResourceLimits` | valid limits; broken limits | green | green | none |\n177|| `internal/clonefidelity` | `ValidDisposition` | 7 dispositions; unknown | green | green | none |\n178|| `internal/clonefidelity` | `ValidReasonCode` | core + reverse-DNS; bad codes | green | green | none |\n179|| `internal/cloneplan` | `BuildProjectionPlan` | valid plan; every invalid class in the clause map | n/a (new) | green | none (new surface, no importer yet) |\n180|| `internal/cloneplan` | `DecodeProjectionPlan` | sealed plan; mutated / hand-built docs | n/a (new) | green | none |\n181|| `internal/cloneplan` | `BuildProjectedObjectManifest` | valid manifest; every invalid class | n/a (new) | green | none |\n182|| `internal/cloneplan` | `DecodeProjectedObjectManifest` | sealed manifest; mutated docs | n/a (new) | green | none |\n183|| `internal/cloneplan` | 5 vocabulary predicates | in-vocabulary; out-of-vocabulary incl. invalid UTF-8 | n/a (new) | green | none |\n184|\n185|## Stated bounds (sibling scope or spec-silent, not waived)\n186|\n187|- `canonical_event_ids` equality with Canonical Session order needs\n188|  the session as an input; only ordered-unique shape is gated here.\n189|- Item-mapping coverage (\"one for every captured/canonical item\")\n190|  needs the manifests as inputs; only the row shape, count, and key\n191|  order are gated here.\n192|- Expected-resource and manifest-entry partitioning against plan\n193|  operations needs the plan as a cross-input; only intra-shape\n194|  rules are gated here.\n195|- Synthesized insertion anchors against canonical IDs need the\n196|  Canonical Session; only digest-or-null shape is gated here.\n197|- `total_bytes` reconciliation is an EXPLICIT STATED BOUND: the\n198|  pinned text states no derivation rule, so any uint53 admits\n199|  (witnessed by\n200|  `TestTotalBytesIsAStatedBoundUntilSpecDefinesDerivation`).\n201|  Owner: spec clarification (agent-session-manager-spec).\n202|- Synthesized array order: array position IS the insertion\n203|  sequence; no order gate is expressible (I12).\n204|- `required_dispositions` key closure is the request owner's bound\n205|  (`sessadapter` checkRequiredDispositions), mirrored exactly (I3).\n206|- `forbid_reasons` admits literal bounded strings (I4), not\n207|  reason-vocabulary members.\n208|- Five-operation DAG coverage is structural, not exhaustive: every\n209|  graph through four operations is enumerated against the oracle,\n210|  and at five operations every edge class is driven at every\n211|  position over the per-edge-local rule pinned by\n212|  `TestDAGLocalityStructure` and `TestDAGSingleEdgeLocality`. The\n213|  full 33M-graph five-operation enumeration is infeasible and is\n214|  not run.\n215|- The no-literal-list guard trips on census-scale composites (at\n216|  least 10 distinct member names at 40%+ member purity); smaller\n217|  literal fragments are below its line by design.\n218|- JSON-level member probes (missing/extra/duplicated/wrong-type/\n219|  case-variant) run at the decode entries; Go inputs cannot express\n220|  an extra, duplicated, or wrong-typed member, so the build-side\n221|  member census is the per-field zero-value sweep\n222|  (`TestBuildZeroValue*`, reflection-count-checked).\n223|- Planning semantics (strategy/profile choice, checkpoint message\n224|  authority, inactive tools/instructions, token metadata) belong to\n225|  the sibling planning leaf (TASK-260924-3n78rv): this leaf gates\n226|  shapes only.\n227|- Sections 13.14.3-13.14.5 and the Read-Back, Validation Report,\n228|  Migration Checkpoint, and Lineage Receipt contracts are sibling\n229|  scope.","final_result":true}}}
